8	
9	/**
10	 * Derives an owner's {@code customerCode} — the owner's region-and-hash identity,
11	 * formatted {@code <REGION>-<HASH8>}:
12	 *
13	 * <ul>
14	 * <li>{@code REGION} is the region code derived from the postcode: look the postcode up
15	 * against the inclusive region ranges (NSW 2000-2099, VIC 3000-3099, QLD 4000-4099) and,
16	 * only when the postcode is absent or in no known range, fall back to the fixed
17	 * city-to-region table (Sydney-&gt;NSW, Melbourne-&gt;VIC, Brisbane-&gt;QLD), else
18	 * {@code UNKNOWN}.</li>
19	 * <li>{@code HASH8} is the first 8 upper-case hex characters of SHA-256 over
20	 * {@code normalizedTelephone + lastName}, where the telephone is normalized to E.164 form
21	 * (an absent or unparseable telephone contributes an empty string).</li>
22	 * </ul>
23	 *
24	 * <p>The whole owner identity — the {@code customerCode} itself, the values built from it
25	 * (membership number and its Luhn check digit), the create audit record and the derived
26	 * locality — flows from this single value. There is no sequence number.
27	 *
28	 * <p>A plain utility (not an OfficeFloor function), so it may expose helpers without
